{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791100577,"nonce":"02Xg6SjbT1eCEiSxz6IDtUw3GoQ=","title":"A state machine engine on signals for components' transient states","message":"User direction (2026-10-04): an FSM engine for complex transient states, as Blinc's Stateful FSM drives its widgets, but on ashui's signals: no stateful closures. A machine's state is a Signal, so data-state, computeds and watches follow it; transitions are a typed match over enum states and events; entry and exit actions; delayed transitions on the AnimationScheduler clock, for transient states (a tooltip waiting to show and closing, an overlay's exit, a toast's life). First user: ashui.components.Tooltip, whose owner is disposed on close before its exit animation plays.","files":null}]}